1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Loop Engine
Loop Engine uses one operational runtime object for every executable graph vertex.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:08,000
One system, four clear parts
Self-improvement is a Practitioner task profile. It is not a fifth system part.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,500
A Loop is one typed operational node
Ports, records, files, edges, and services are not additional operational node types.

4
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:15,000
Input, work, validated output
Schema version, shape, optionality, units, and encoding belong in the port contract.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,800
Definition first, instance second
A graph vertex should resolve to an exact definition ID, version, and content digest.

6
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:22,000
Deterministic
A deterministic Loop records zero physical model calls.

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,400
Hybrid
The model path is optional. If used, its physical call and usage must be recorded.

8
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:28,800
Non-deterministic or LLM-driven
A mode label without a physical model attempt is not model-led execution.

9
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:33,300
Each Loop instance selects one mode
A deterministic Loop can spawn a non-deterministic Loop, and the reverse is also valid when permissions allow it.

10
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:37,500
One Loop runtime, three role branches
A spawned Loop is still the same runtime type. Its role profile states why it exists.

11
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:41,500
A Practitioner Loop decides what work is useful next
The Loop repeats only while its loop condition is true and its budget allows more work.

12
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:45,700
A Practitioner can spawn focused Loops
Private context stays isolated. Typed results return to the Loop that requested the work.

13
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:49,700
Every Loop should access the same three shared groups
Permissions decide which service operations are available. A run mode never expands authority.

14
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:53,700
Intelligence is organized by what it contributes
Runtime Memory is separate. It is temporary and lasts only for the current run.

15
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:57,200
Context Intelligence
Search returns a small typed reference. A Retrieved Context Intelligence Loop materializes the selected content.

16
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:00,700
Code Intelligence
Discovery is effect-free. Invocation begins after selection, compatibility checks, and permission checks.

17
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:04,300
Runtime History and Solution Intelligence
Intelligence Loops search, replay, or compare exact saved records. Missing evidence remains visible.

18
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:07,800
User Feedback Intelligence
A deterministic Loop can return exact guidance. An authorized model-led Loop can frame it for the current task.

19
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:12,300
The Solution Canvas keeps several working routes
Selection, fallback, routing, and ensembles must be explicit Solution Loops, not hidden edge behavior.

20
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:16,800
Loops connect into one typed directed acyclic graph
Starting, Spawned by, Queried by, Retrieved by, and Connected from describe different relationships.

21
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:21,000
Static Architecture has three public groups
The groups provide reusable access. They are not additional operational nodes.

22
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,200
From public websites to a tested model
Every executable step is a Loop with its own typed ports, selected mode, conditions, and history.

23
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:29,400
Find reliable sources and inspect every PDF
Discovery remains effect-free. Network and file operations start only after exact permission checks.

24
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:33,600
Build trusted data before building models
Competing model candidates remain separate until an independent verifier compares them.

25
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:38,100
Verify, repair, compile, and record
The selected Solution graph enters the Canvas. The same ordered events power live view and playback.

26
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:43,100
Self-improvement uses the same Practitioner Loop
The architecture is clear. The remaining work is to consolidate the runtime and prove one real end-to-end task.

